WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.860
Last weekend, Music
and Theater Arts

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.360
had a series of events
that were happening.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.725
They put up a live
stream online.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.700
When a friend told me our
video had 14,000 views,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.230
I was like, blown away.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.030
Puts pressure on in a good
way to know that there

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.650
are that many people watching.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.010
Does have implicit feel of
being a much larger arena.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:43.830
It was like, oh, greetings from
Rome, greetings from Brazil.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:47.540
I think it was great to show
people that MIT wasn't limited

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.800
to just technology.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.166
We're doing arts
plus technology.

00:00:53.166 --> 00:00:54.540
My parents got to
watch it, which

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.370
was really awesome, because
they live in California.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.491
So it's not really feasible
for them to fly all the way out

00:01:00.491 --> 00:01:00.990
here.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.640
And so they were
very, very happy

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.650
and sent me lots of
texts at the end.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.540
Most of the students
who come to MIT--

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.454
they have a
performance background.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.090
I did not expect this
is as a high school

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.730
student coming to like a
science and math school.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:27.060
I kind of felt like I was almost
making a sacrifice of music

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.080
to come here.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.470
And so finding out that there's
so much support and energy

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.482
and money that goes into this
is really, really wonderful.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:45.200
It's pretty sublime,
I guess you could say.

